      "body": "`sequence_tiled_compute(..., output_reduction=\"mean\")` rescales the gradient of any other term added to the same loss.\n\n**Cause:** `SequenceTiledCompute.backward` ran `incoming_grad /= shards` on the gradient autograd passes in. For `tiled + other`, both branches receive that same tensor, so the other term's gradient was divided by `shards`.\n\n**Fix:** divide out of place. `TiledMLP` never mutates its incoming gradient, and `TiledFusedLogitsLoss` divides its own tensor, so neither has this defect.\n\n**Not a duplicate:** no open or closed PR or issue mentions `SequenceTiledCompute`, `sequence_tiled_compute` or `incoming_grad`.\n\n**Test:** `DS_ACCELERATOR=cpu pytest tests/unit/ulysses_alst/test_tiled_compute.py -k \"not Distributed and not TestTiledFusedLogitsLoss and not TestTiledMLP and not test_tiled_mlp\" -q` on CPU only (Apple M2 Pro, torch 2.11.0). The new test sums the tiled result with `x.sum()` in both orders: it fails before (max diff 0.75) and 26 pass after. Not covered: GPU, the `DistributedTest` cases, ZeRO stages, multi-rank sequence parallelism.\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
